  "headline": "The City of Dreams",
  "short_description": "India's financial capital and home of Bollywood, Mumbai mixes colonial-era landmarks with a fast-paced modern skyline.",
  "about": "Built across seven islands reclaimed into one landmass, Mumbai is India's largest city by population and its commercial and entertainment hub.\n\nA coastal city on the Arabian Sea in western Maharashtra, prone to monsoon flooding.\n\nHome to Bollywood, a cosmopolitan food scene and landmark colonial and Art Deco architecture.\n\nHighly diverse — major temples, mosques, churches, synagogues and the Haji Ali Dargah coexist.",
  "history": "Grew from a Portuguese and then British trading post into India's leading port and industrial city; the islands were progressively joined through land reclamation.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj International Airport (airport)\n- Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus (railway)\n- Mumbai Central Bus Depot (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Marathi, Hindi, English\nBudget: premium",
  "best_time_text": "November to February",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2–3 days",
